# bin/scrub-gate token list -- EXAMPLE. Every name below is invented.
#
# This file is documentation, not a source. scrub-gate does NOT read it: a
# gate running on example tokens would find nothing in a real repository and
# report exit 0, which is the one thing it must never do. Copy it, fill it in
# with the names you actually need kept out of a public repository, and put
# the copy where a private overlay supplies it:
#
#   <overlay>/scrub-gate/tokens                    (before stow)
#   ~/.config/scrub-gate/tokens.d/<overlay-name>   (after stow)
#
# or point $SCRUB_GATE_TOKENS straight at it for a one-off run.
#
# FORMAT
#   One extended-regex fragment per line, joined with | in the order read.
#   Blank lines and # comments are ignored; leading and trailing whitespace is
#   stripped, so a fragment may contain a space but may not begin or end with
#   one. Matching is case-insensitive, so write each name once, in any case.
#   A literal dot must be escaped -- `example\.com`, not `example.com`, which
#   would also match `exampleXcom`.
#
# CHOOSING FRAGMENTS
#   Whole identifiers, never bare prefixes. Check each one against your own
#   username and $HOME first: if your login were `acme_jo`, the fragment
#   `acme_` would match every absolute path on the machine, bury the real
#   findings, and get the gate switched off within a day. That is why the list
#   below names `acme_nav` and `acme_hmi` rather than `acme_`.
#   tests/test_scrub_gate.sh enforces this against the real username.
#
#   Prefer a few narrow, high-signal names over a wide net. False positives
#   are loud and cheap; a missed name is silent and permanent.

# the company, run together and spaced
acmerobotics
Acme Robotics

# source repositories and package prefixes
acme-ros
acme_ros
acme_nav
acme_hmi
libacme

# build environments
acme-build
acme-debug
acme-stage

# infrastructure: CI host, internal range, VPN profile, build agent
ci\.internal\.example
10\.99\.0
AcmeVPN
builder-amd-agent

# issue tracker keys, anchored to a following digit so only real keys match
ACME-[0-9]

# mail domain
acme\.example

# third parties whose name would identify the employer by association
fablift
